 ```
+
+### `applyPatch(document, patch)`
+
+Applies a [JSON Patch](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6902) (RFC 6902) — an array of `add`, `remove`,
+`replace`, `move`, `copy` and `test` operations — to a JSON document and returns the resulting document
+as a new value; it does not mutate `document` or `patch`. Throws if the patch is not syntactically
+valid, or if one of its operations fails against `document`.
+
+```ts
+import { applyPatch } from "json-toolkit";
+
+const document = { foo: "bar", list: [1, 2] };
+
+applyPatch(document, [
+  { op: "replace", path: "/foo", value: "baz" },
+  { op: "add", path: "/list/-", value: 3 },
+]); // { foo: "baz", list: [1, 2, 3] }
+```
